---
import EnterpriseDetail from '../../components/enterprise/EnterpriseDetail.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/ComparisonTable.astro';
import ShotFrame from '../../components/ShotFrame.astro';
---

<EnterpriseDetail
  slug="cost-control"
  seoTitle="Cost Controls | SAM Enterprise"
  seoDescription="SAM has no fee of its own: you pay Cloudflare, your cloud providers and your model providers directly. Per-user AI budgets, vCPU-hour quotas and an admin cost page."
  title="Three bills you already understand"
  subtitle="SAM is free, open-source software, so there is no SAM invoice. You pay Cloudflare for the control plane, your cloud providers for machines and your model providers for tokens, each at your own rates."
>
  <h2>Where the money goes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: the Workers Paid plan plus usage for the control plane, storage and any Instant sessions.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud providers</strong>: machines and volumes, billed by Hetzner, Scaleway, Vultr, Infomaniak, DigitalOcean, UpCloud or Google Cloud to whichever account SAM used.</li>
    <li><strong>Model providers</strong>: each user's API keys or subscriptions, or the installation AI proxy's account if you turn it on.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Machines are shared where possible: placement packs a user's workspaces onto machines that have room, and
    empty machines are deleted after a warm period.
  </p>

  <h2>Budgets and quotas</h2>
  <ComparisonTable
    caption="Controls and what they cover."
    rowHeader="Control"
    columns={['Set by', 'Covers']}
    rows={[
      { label: 'Daily token limit', cells: ['Each user, up to an admin ceiling', 'Model traffic through the installation AI proxy'] },
      { label: 'Monthly cost cap', cells: ['Each user, up to an admin ceiling', 'Model traffic through the installation AI proxy'] },
      { label: 'Compute quota', cells: ['Admins (default and per user)', 'vCPU-hours a month on installation-provided cloud accounts'] },
      { label: 'Agent AI budget', cells: ['Project settings', 'Workers AI calls agents make as a tool, $5 a month by default'] },
    ]}
  />
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      Model traffic that goes straight from an agent to a provider with the user's own key or subscription is not
      metered by SAM. The provider's console is the source of truth for that spend. Machines on a user's or
      project's own cloud account do not count against the compute quota.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ShotFrame
    src="/images/features/sam-usage-tokens.png"
    alt="Settings, Usage: token usage and cost per model, a per-day usage chart, and progress against a monthly budget."
    caption="Each user sees their proxied AI usage by model and by day, against their monthly budget."
  />

  <h2>The admin cost page</h2>
  <p>
    Admin → Costs shows proxied model spend by model, day and user, with a projection, next to an estimate of
    compute cost. The compute figure is vCPU-hours times a configured rate, not your cloud invoice. Admin → Usage
    breaks compute down per user.
  </p>
  <ShotFrame
    src="/images/features/sam-admin-costs.png"
    alt="Admin, Costs: month-to-date model cost, a monthly projection, estimated compute cost from vCPU-hours, a daily cost chart, cost by model and model cost by user."
    caption="Admin → Costs: proxied model spend with a projection, plus estimated compute cost."
  />
</EnterpriseDetail>
